
### Casos de prueba:
### 1- Inscripción exitosa → email recibido (201)
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "juanbautistajrsabadu@gmail.com",
    "password": "juan1234"
}

### Creamos un ticket nuevo -> Deberia devolver 201
POST http://localhost:9909/api/events/6abf01469cf194bbd75a47a9/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "quantity": 6
}

###
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/logout
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2- Inscripción sin sesión → 401
POST http://localhost:9909/api/events/6abf07369cf194bbd75a47ac/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "quantity": 1
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3- Inscripción a evento inexistente → 404
### Me logueo
POST http://localhost:9909/api/sessions/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "juanbautistajrsabadu@gmail.com",
    "password": "juan1234"
}

### El ID no pertenee a un evento existente dentro de la base de datos
POST http://localhost:9909/api/events/6abf07369cf194bbd75a4700/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "quantity": 1
}

